---
/**
 * Terms of Service. Source draft: docs/paddle/terms.md (keep the two in sync).
 * Not legal advice: a lawyer reviews it before the live Paddle account. Paddle requires: the legal name exactly as on
 * the Paddle account, Paddle named as merchant of record (section 3), and a link to the refund policy.
 */
import LegalShell from "../components/pages/LegalShell.astro";
import { PRICING } from "../config/pricing";
import { SITE } from "../config/site";
import { useCopy } from "../content/copy";
const { copy: COPY } = useCopy(Astro.url);
const l = COPY.legalPage;
const mail = SITE.email;
---

<LegalShell title="Terms of Service" description="The terms for using tadamevents.com and buying a Tadam! game: payment through Paddle, refunds, your content and how long we keep it." updatedLine="Last updated: November 25, 2026">

  <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#who">Who we are</a></li>
      <li><a href="#service">The Service</a></li>
      <li><a href="#payment">Ordering and payment</a></li>
      <li><a href="#refunds">Refunds</a></li>
      <li><a href="#eligibility">Who can use the Service</a></li>
      <li><a href="#content">Your content</a></li>
      <li><a href="#game">Your game</a></li>
      <li><a href="#retention">How long we keep your game</a></li>
      <li><a href="#availability">Availability</a></li>
      <li><a href="#liability">Liability</a></li>
      <li><a href="#changes">Changes to these terms</a></li>
      <li><a href="#law">Governing law</a></li>
      <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <section id="who">
    <h2 class="display">1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Tadam! ("Tadam", "we", "us") is operated by {l.legalName}, a sole trader. Contact:
      {" "}<a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      These terms apply to your use of tadamevents.com and to every game you create or buy there (the "Service"). By
      creating a game or making a purchase, you agree to these terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="service">
    <h2 class="display">2. The Service</h2>
    <p>
      Tadam is an online tool for creating a personalized trivia game show for a party or event. You provide stories,
      details and photos; the Service drafts questions, lets you choose a ready-made host and voice or create a custom host with VIP, and lets you review
      and edit the game. After payment, the finished game is delivered by email as a private link, usually within 24
      hours. The game is played in a web browser: the host appears on a big screen and guests answer from their phones.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some parts of the game, such as draft questions, the host's voice and the host's video, are produced with the help
      of automated and AI tools. You can review the delivered game and use the question edits included in your package before you play.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="payment">
    <h2 class="display">3. Ordering and payment</h2>
    <p>
      Our order process is conducted by our online reseller Paddle.com. Paddle.com is the Merchant of Record for all our
      orders. Paddle provides all customer service inquiries related to payment and handles returns. Paddle's
      {" "}<a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/checkout-buyer-terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Buyer Terms</a> apply to
      your purchase.
    </p>
    <p>
      Prices are shown on our site before you buy. Sales tax or VAT is calculated by Paddle at checkout based on your
      location.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="refunds">
    <h2 class="display">4. Refunds</h2>
    <p>You can request a full refund within 14 days of purchase. See our <a href="/refunds">Refund Policy</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="eligibility">
    <h2 class="display">5. Who can use the Service</h2>
    <p>
      You must be at least 18 years old to create a game or make a purchase. The Service is meant for adults organizing
      events; children may play the game as guests, but they may not create an account or place an order.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="content">
    <h2 class="display">6. Your content</h2>
    <p>"Your content" means everything you upload or write: stories, names, details, photos, recordings and answers.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>You keep ownership</strong> of your content. You give us a limited license to store, process and display
        it only to create, deliver and support your game, for as long as we keep it (see section 8).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You have the right to use it.</strong> You confirm that you have the permission of every person who
        appears in or is described in your content, and, for children, the permission of their parent or legal guardian.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Nothing harmful.</strong> Your content must not be unlawful, hateful, harassing, sexual, defamatory, or
        meant to humiliate anyone, and must not infringe anyone's rights.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Permission for custom hosts.</strong> You must have a person's explicit permission before using their face
        or voice for a custom host. For anyone under 18, you must have their parent's or legal guardian's permission.
        Do not use a custom host to deceive others or impersonate someone without their permission.
      </li>
      <li>We may refuse, edit out or remove content that breaks these rules, and may cancel the order with a full refund.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="game">
    <h2 class="display">7. Your game</h2>
    <p>
      Once paid, you may play your game at your event and share the private link with your guests, for personal,
      non-commercial use. The hosts, voices, music, design and software remain ours or our licensors'. Do not copy,
      resell or redistribute the game or any part of the Service.
    </p>
    <p>Anyone with the link can open the game. Share it only with people you trust.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="retention">
    <h2 class="display">8. How long we keep your game</h2>
    <p>
      Your game link works for <strong>{PRICING.linkDays} days with Basic or {PRICING.vipLinkDays} days with VIP</strong>
      from delivery. At the end of that period, the game and your content are deleted and the link stops working. You can ask us to delete them earlier at any time by writing to
      {" "}<a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>. Details are in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="availability">
    <h2 class="display">9. Availability</h2>
    <p>
      We work to keep the Service available, but we can't guarantee that it will be uninterrupted or error-free. The game
      needs a working internet connection, a modern browser and a screen at your event; you're responsible for that
      equipment. We recommend testing your game before the event.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="liability">
    <h2 class="display">10. Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent allowed by law, the Service is provided "as is". Our total liability for any claim related to
      the Service is limited to the amount you paid for the game in question. We are not liable for indirect or
      consequential losses. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have as a consumer that cannot be limited by law,
      including your statutory rights in the EU and UK.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2 class="display">11. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms. The version in force when you place an order applies to that order. The date at the top
      shows the latest version.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="law">
    <h2 class="display">12. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      If you are a consumer, you keep the protection of the mandatory consumer laws of the country where you live, and you
      may bring a claim in your local courts.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2 class="display">13. Contact</h2>
    <ul class="contact">
      <li>{l.legalName}</li>
      <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</LegalShell>
